      "content": "I'm truly sorry to hear that you're feeling this profoundly alone and like your life's purpose has been stolen. Loss of identity, especially when it's so integral to who we are, can be indescribably painful. However, your life has yet to end, and within this chapter, there's still much that can be explored. Therapy, especially therapies focused on trauma and post-injury identity, might provide a new narrative for your life. You might discover new ways to find fulfillment and meaning outside of the expectations you had when you were able-bodied. Remember, your worth isn't tied to past abilities or achievements, but to the depth of your experiences and the resilience of your spirit. If you're open to it, I can help you look into counseling services or support groups that specialize in these topics.",
